# Notice — Network Security Monitor

Web-based tool for visualizing, analyzing, and investigating IDS network traffic logs.

## Setup

    python3 -m venv --without-pip venv
    source venv/bin/activate
    curl -sS https://bootstrap.pypa.io/get-pip.py | python3
    pip install -r requirements.txt

## Run

    source venv/bin/activate
    python3 app.py

Open https://localhost:8080 (self-signed cert, accept the warning)

To disable HTTPS:

    python3 app.py --no-ssl

## Configuration

Environment variables:

    EVE_LOG      Path to eve.json (default: /var/log/suricata/eve.json)
    PORT         Server port (default: 8080)
    MAX_LINES    Max log lines to parse from tail (default: 200000)

## Features

### Network Graph
- Interactive D3.js force-directed graph
- Internal (green) vs external (amber) host classification
- Alert-associated nodes/links in red
- Click to isolate connections, drag, zoom, filter by IP

### Security Events
- IDS alert dashboard with severity breakdown
- Timeline view, top signatures, full alert log

### Plaintext Detection
- HTTP (port 80), FTP (credentials visible!), SMTP
- Weak SNMP communities (public, private, iiit123)
- Deprecated TLS (v1.0, v1.1)

### IP Investigation
- Full activity timeline for any IP address
- Risk indicators, connections, DNS queries, TLS sessions
- SSH events (detects Nmap scanning), file transfers

### Anomaly Detection
- Nmap scanning detection
- High-volume flow identification (>50MB)
- DNS anomalies (long domains, NXDOMAIN floods)
- Deprecated TLS, unusual ports, app-layer anomalies

### Asset Management
- Identified vs unidentified internal host tracking
- Coverage percentage bar
- Register, edit, delete assets with owner/hostname/department
- One-click investigate or register from unidentified list

### Incident Management
- Create cases with severity and status tracking
- Attach events and investigation notes
- Status workflow: Open > Investigating > Resolved > Closed

### Policy Engine
- 6 default rules (no plaintext HTTP, no FTP, weak SNMP, etc.)
- On-demand policy scan with violation detection
- Create incidents from violations

## HTTPS

Self-signed certificate is auto-generated in certs/ on first setup.
To regenerate:

    openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout certs/key.pem \
      -out certs/cert.pem -days 365 -nodes -subj "/CN=notice.local"

## Project Structure

    app.py               Bottle entry point, HTTPS server
    eve_reader.py        Shared eve.json reader (tail_lines, iter_events)
    db.py                SQLite schema, cache, default seeds
    analyzers/
      plaintext.py       Plaintext protocol detection
      anomaly.py         Anomaly detection engine
      policy.py          Policy rule evaluation
    routes/
      graph.py           /api/graph, /api/summary
      security.py        /api/alerts
      plaintext.py       /api/plaintext
      investigate.py     /api/investigate/<ip>
      anomalies.py       /api/anomalies
      incidents.py       /api/incidents (CRUD)
      policies.py        /api/policies, /api/policies/scan
      assets.py          /api/assets, /api/assets/discovery
    static/
      index.html         Tabbed SPA (8 views)
    certs/               Self-signed TLS certificate
    requirements.txt     Python dependencies (bottle)
    venv/                Python virtual environment
